      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n1. **Pre-write recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if the file existed) or a note that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or all writes being denied), the journal can reverse all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting any newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-nothing semantics**: This mechanism provides each run with all-or-nothing write semantics without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent note**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use this rollback capability since it has no write tool, but the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library for use by agents that do write.",
      "input_tokens": 5362,
      "output_tokens": 249
    }
